Yes, unless you're a priest you won't automatically know the
blessed/cursed status of anything you get from wishes, and you won't
know the pluses unless you identify it (unless it's armor, which
identifies its pluses when you put it on).  However, I believe that
Excalibur is _always_ rustproof, whether you wish for it, #dip for it,
or find it.

I've heard that people prefer to wish for +2 items rather than +3 so
that they can get it up to +5 with enchant armor scrolls more easily -
in fact I've seen elaborate descriptions of how to get armor and
weapons to the max without blowing them up, but these assume you have
tons of scrolls and nothing else to do in the game... but I digress. 
The point is, with a weapon like Excalibur or Mjollnir (with or without
gauntlets, it's +24 damage) you're already doing pretty well even if
it's not at +7.

